{"agent_id":"pp3g-A1hS-synthesis-of-observer-adversarial-reviews-read-only","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-26T23:12:55.858142998Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"06add12a-3a8f-4873-b335-861975dbf512","comment_uuid":"f871b067-eb4f-4e59-a331-3a860b1ad9a7","author":"pp3g-A1hS-synthesis-of-observer-adversarial-reviews-read-only","content":"Result: Synthesis of Observer adversarial reviews #465, #466, #467, #469, #470 (plus #466 follow-ups Pn6g latest) — read-only registry + disposition + design implications\n\nMethod: pulled --kind result verdicts from 5 issues via crosslink issue show (hydrate). Skipped 6T4f Nemotron (timed-out, per dispatch). Normalized severities, deduplicated by underlying mechanism (40+ raw findings → 31 deduplicated rows). F24 ephemerality promoted MINOR→MAJOR per operator directive (ephemeral Observer memory = unreliable). Evidence lines cited at latest HEAD (observer.sh 3310L post-fixpass) where Pn6g re-verified; older line refs preserved where still applicable. #470 (deep-research-423 claim verification, 26 adjudications, AGREE on all) is out-of-scope for Observer code and excluded from registry — noted §0.\n\nWHY: operator needs a single prioritized registry to gate unsupervised operation (MUST now) vs high-value low-cost (SHOULD now) vs v2/v3.\nWHAT: deduplication of every finding with source, severity, file:line, path, disposition + design implications for F23/F24/F4 vs finite-state/explicit-contract principles.\nHOW CERTAIN: evidence-based (line-level citations, Pn6g arithmetic proofs, live CWD rc=1 demonstration, harness 96/98→181/181 trajectories). Deduplication judged by mechanism, not label.\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: same as reviewers — non-dry-run mutations end-to-end, rclone positive-path remote, RED verification fault injection, long-duration loops, concurrent-instance lock demonstration (code asserted), opencode.log retry-after formats in the wild, tamper attack, live DB schema drift.\n\n---\n§0 — Verdict headline summary\n\n| Issue | Reviewer | Verdict | Raw findings | Headline |\n|-------|----------|---------|--------------|----------|\n| #465 | pp3g-ccRh | CONDITIONAL (release-blocked CRITICAL F1 + 8 MAJOR) | 18 (1 CRITICAL, 8 MAJOR, 8 MINOR + F18 assumption) | CWD defect blocks all mutations; kill without confirmation; tamper; backup gaps |\n| #466 r1 | pp3g-GpoH | CONDITIONAL (7 MAJOR) | 21 (7 MAJOR, 14 MINOR) | Parked-expiry, backup integrity, ungated cleanup, breaker starvation, crash duplicate, no lock, R2 untested |\n| #466 r1-verify | pp3g-O8rg | ACCEPT-FOR-SHAKEDOWN (4 CLOSED /1 PARTIAL /1 NOT-CLOSED) | fix-pass audit | F1/F2/F3/F6 CLOSED, F5 PARTIAL, F4 NOT-CLOSED (gating) |\n| #466 r2 (latest Pn6g) | pp3g-Pn6g | CONDITIONAL (1 MAJOR + 2 MINOR new; 2 still-OPEN priors) | 3 new (F22 MAJOR, F23 MINOR, F24 MINOR→MAJOR) | Backup retry ~57m not 15m; backup blocks loop 5-10m; ephemeral/tamper surface |\n| #467 | pp3g-f8fx | CONDITIONAL (2 MAJOR) | 12 (2 MAJOR, 7 MINOR, 3 withdrawn) | Fragile CLI output parsing (locks check, issue show) |\n| #469 | pp3g-3Q1d | CONDITIONAL (4 CRITICAL 5 MAJOR 8 MINOR) | 17 (4 CRITICAL, 5 MAJOR, 8 MINOR) | Missing set -e, unbounded growth, rclone OOM, regex gaps, quoting risk, error cap |\n| #470 | pp3g-2QW7 | AGREE on all 26 | 26 claim adjudications (20 VERIFIED 3 PARTIAL 2 REFUTED 1 UNVERIFIABLE) | Doom_loop/R2/off-server claims — out-of-scope for Observer, no registry row |\n\nAll four Observer reviewers: CONDITIONAL. Unanimous: F1-F6 feature set genuinely implemented, architecture sound (out-of-process, state-owned, CLI-mediated, convergent-evidence gate), harness strong (96/98 → 181/181), but NOT trusted unsupervised. #470 confirms fact-check methodology but does not change Observer disposition.\n\n---\n§1 — Deduplicated registry (Finding | Source reviews | Severity | Evidence file:line | Affected path | Disposition)\n\nSeverity key: CRITICAL = data-destroying or total-function loss in default config. MAJOR = safety/integrity gap that can silently lose data or disarm kill authority (blocks unsupervised if MUST now). MINOR = low blast-radius, hygiene, or unlikely edge. F24 shown as MAJOR (operator override; reviewers labeled MINOR).\n\n| ID | Finding (deduplicated) | Source reviews | Severity | Evidence file:line | Affected path | Disposition |\n|----|------------------------|----------------|----------|--------------------|---------------|-------------|\n| R01 | **Breaker starvation — single rolling window gates comments AND lethal actions (kill/cleanup)**. Alert storm (admission, fast-path UNKNOWN, doctrine) exhausts 24/hr budget → frozen-agent stop/cleanup silently skipped (returns False). Dedup reduces volume but diverse failures still starve safety budget. | #466 F4 (GpoH, still OPEN per Pn6g prior-F4), #465 F2 (phase-before-mutation compounds), #469-10 (cap only tracks liveness) | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:473-488 `breaker_allow`, 495 `post_comment`, 830 `kickoff_cleanup`, 847 `kickoff_stop`, 1117-1157 `act_frozen` (still reports FAILED when breaker blocks) | scripts/observer/observer.sh:breaker_allow | **MUST now** — blocks unsupervised. Fix: reserve safety budget (e.g., 24 total / 20 general + 4 reserved for stop/cleanup) or separate breaker pools; low-cost, highest leverage before unsupervised. |\n| R02 | **Terminal phase marked BEFORE mutation confirmed → transient breaker/timeout never retried**. `rec[\"phase\"]=\"frozen-handled\"` etc. set regardless of kickoff_stop/cleanup rc; next cycle skips LIKELY-FROZEN branch. | #465 F2 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:1124-1129 `act_frozen`, 1090-1094 `act_killed`, 949-967 `act_completed` | scripts/observer/observer.sh:act_* phase guards | **MUST now** — blocks reliable kill/cleanup. Fix: gate phase advance on mutation success; on breaker-block/timeout keep phase retryable (e.g., `phase=\"frozen-pending-retry\"`), re-drive next cycle. Low-cost reorder. |\n| R03 | **LIKELY-FROZEN immediate kill with no independent aliveness re-check & no 2-cycle confirmation**. Fires on first occurrence; never calls `pane_status` before `kickoff_stop`, unlike DEAD-UNMARKED which does. Misclassification by liveness scanner (out-of-scope) → immediate kill of healthy agent. Design required ≥2-cycle confirmation. | #465 F4 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:1290-1298 `process_agent` LIKELY-FROZEN branch, 1117-1157 `act_frozen` (no pane check), vs 1039-1055 `classify_death` pane verify | scripts/observer/observer.sh:process_agent/act_frozen | **MUST now** — weakest-evidence kill path besides parked-expiry. Fix: 2-cycle counter or `pane_status != alive` gate before kill; small counter dict. |\n| R04 | **Parked-expiry auto-kill without re-verification & resume_at misparse** (bare-seconds, UTC assumption, stale-tail re-park → immediate expiry). | #466 F1, #465 F4, #469-8 (retry-after coverage) | **MAJOR** | old: observer.sh:1237-1243, 587-615 `parse_retry_after`, 1159-1179 `act_parked` | scripts/observer/observer.sh:parse_retry_after/act_parked | **DO NOT CHANGE** (CLOSED per fix-pass). Verified at Pn6g: fixed 1839-1865 (re-scan log tail, extend park `resume_at=max(parsed, now+grace_floor)`, kill requires expiry AND clean tail); T5 covers both paths. Keep. |\n| R05 | **Off-server backup integrity gap — watermark advances before remote verify; only index remote-verified; sync failure no retry backlog**. Header/F4(d) claim overstates code; server-loss = silent permanent archive gap for failed window. Last_run_ts stamped before work → failed pass waits full interval. | #466 F2, #465 F7/F9 | **MAJOR** | old: observer.sh:2046-2069 watermark advance, 2080-2092 rclone, 1934-1964 index-only cat, 1971-1976 last_run_ts before work | scripts/observer/observer.sh:wave_backup/rclone_sync_and_verify | **DO NOT CHANGE** (CLOSED per fix-pass). Pn6g: fixed 2738-2806 (commit_watermarks only on GREEN/local-ack, sync RED holds ALL watermarks + backlog retried, last_run_ts re-stamped with retry offset). Residual: export gzip artefacts still only locally verified (index remote-only) → track as DEFER (R05b). |\n| R06 | **Crash between action execution and save_state → duplicate kills/cleanups/comments**. State saves only at cycle end; any exception (evidence compose, export, TypeError on tampered fastpath_seen) → bash `cycle-program-failed` with state untouched → next cycle re-fires. | #466 F5, #465 F5 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:2319-2437 main(), 2424 save_state, 2447-2488 bash wrapper; Pn6g 3148-3158,3172-3182 cap | scripts/observer/observer.sh:main/save_state | **DEFER to v2** — fix-pass PARTIAL mitigation shipped (save failure rc=2 + bump_error → consecutive-error cap halts loop; blast radius 1 duplicate then halt). True idempotency needs checkpointing/idempotency keys (architectural). Acceptable for supervised shakedown; require before unsupervised v2. |\n| R07 | **No single-instance guard — last-writer-wins state with kill authority**. Documented detached tmux loop; double-launch yields interleaved kills/comments with each seeing own breaker state. | #466 F6, #467 cross-cutting races, #469 implicit | **MAJOR** | old: none; fixed: observer.sh:3195-3244 | scripts/observer/observer.sh:instance lock (new) | **DO NOT CHANGE** (CLOSED). Fix-pass: O_EXCL noclobber + PID content + `ps -p` stale detection + LOCK_OWNED trap (T19 live-refusal + stale-recovery PASS). Keep. |\n| R08 | **R2 deliverable-check rebuild has zero harness coverage (merge-base/diff/cat-file -e loop never executed)**. T1/T12 only check staging row; REPO_ROOT pointed at nonexistent dir so all git paths short-circuit. | #466 F7 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:887-936 `deliverable_check` (918-931 cat-file -e loop), run-tests.sh grep 0 assertions | scripts/observer/tests/run-tests.sh / observer.sh:deliverable_check | **DO NOT CHANGE** (RESOLVED per Pn6g). T1 now asserts \"Deliverable verified\" path + T18a/T18b (no branch / empty branch) both preserve worktree; contract-level coverage achieved. Mechanics-level assertion can DEFER. |\n| R09 | **Cleanup-on-COMPLETED ungated on deliverable — automates #460 lost-work class** (builder writes DONE with uncommitted work → kickoff_cleanup destroys worktree, deliverable_check then reports files_changed=0 over corpse). | #466 F3 | **MAJOR** | old: observer.sh:942-979 (cleanup before deliverable_check) | scripts/observer/observer.sh:act_completed | **DO NOT CHANGE** (CLOSED). Fixed 1318-1414 (deliverable_check FIRST; cleanup only if deliverable_present; else flag_for_sweep + cleanup_skipped + staging `skipped-unverified-deliverable`); T18a/b PASS. Keep. |\n| R10 | **All crosslink invocations depend on launch CWD; outside repo they silently no-op (rc=1 \"Not a crosslink repository\")** → cleanup/kill/comments/admission/hub-position inert. Documented `tmux new-session -d bash observer.sh` inherits launcher CWD. | #465 F1 (CRITICAL), #466 F20 / #465 F15 T16 non-hermetic demonstrates | **CRITICAL** | observer.sh:501 post_comment, 837 kickoff_cleanup, 854 kickoff_stop, 2261 issue show, 2269 locks check, 764 last_hub_position; run-tests.sh:483-488 T16 96/98 vs 98/98 | scripts/observer/observer.sh (all crosslink calls) | **MUST now** — total function loss in real deployment. Fix: `cd \"$REPO_ROOT\"` after discovery in bash wrapper (or pass --repo / CROSSLINK_REPO env); one-line, blocks supervised shakedown correctness. |\n| R11 | **Slug-substring attribution collision** — `directory=[^\\t ]*<esc>` matches longer slug's path, stealing session IDs → wrong evidence attached, mis-attributed death/rate-limit. | #465 F3 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:538-539 primary, 542 fallback `cwd=[...]`, `esc=re.escape(agent)` unanchored | scripts/observer/observer.sh:agent_log_section | **SHOULD now** — low-cost anchor to path component (`*/<slug>(?=\\s\\|$)`) fixes misattribution; strong value before large swarm. |\n| R12 | **/tmp tamper surface + symlink + world-readable evidence** — state dir default perms, atomic write via `open(tmp,\"w\")` follows symlinks → arbitrary overwrite via os.replace; any local user can mark agents handled (suppress kill) or read log tails. | #465 F6, #469-12, #467 tamper note, #466 F15 | **MAJOR** (was CRITICAL in #469) | observer.sh:300 `mkdir -p` no mode, 459-463 atomic write (`open(tmp,\"w\")`), 695 evidence bundles world-readable, 902-925 bundle write | /tmp/opencode/observer-state + evidence bundles | **SHOULD now** — chmod 700 state dir, use `os.open(O_EXCL\\|O_NOFOLLOW)` or per-run secure temp, restrict evidence perms; low-cost, closes suppress-kill vector. Full WORM/external anchoring → DEFER. |\n| R13 | **Schema-dependent silent zero-export** — only `session`/`session_v2` with exact columns matched; live store drift (e.g., session_v3, renamed columns) → export loop never runs, pass appears to succeed, no GREEN/RED. | #465 F8, #469-16 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:1827-1841 `snapshot_session_tables`, 1831-1838 column filter | scripts/observer/observer.sh:snapshot_session_tables | **SHOULD now** — add explicit \"no session table found → RED + alert\" path; low-cost, closes silent retention gap. |\n| R14 | **rclone index hash loads entire index into memory (`fh.read()`) → OOM on large deployment (10k+ sessions)**. Index grows per exported row. | #469-5 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:1956-1960 `fh.read()` stream hash | scripts/observer/observer.sh:rclone_sync_and_verify | **SHOULD now** — stream hash via `hashlib.sha256` chunked read or `rclone hashsum`; low-cost. |\n| R15 | **Hardcoded `main` branch — repos with different default branch silently mis-report deliverable/merged/push-ahead**. | #465 F10 | **MINOR** (borderline MAJOR for forks) | observer.sh:914 `merge-base main`, 932 `is-ancestor branch main`, 1354 `refs/heads/main`, 743 `diff --stat main` | scripts/observer/observer.sh:deliverable_check/wave_merge/worktree_git_evidence | **SHOULD now** — make base branch configurable (OBSERVER_BASE_BRANCH, default `main` with `origin/HEAD` fallback); trivial. |\n| R16 | **Backup retry backoff miscomputes ~57m not 15m** — formula `now - INTERVAL + RETRY` with gate `now - last_run < INTERVAL` keeps 57m of INTERVAL remaining; comment and var name promise 15m. Operator tuning RETRY is illusory. | #466 Pn6g F22 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:2620 gate `time.time() - last_run_ts < 86400`, 2861-2865 re-stamp `last_run_ts = now - INTERVAL_MINS*60 + RETRY_MINS*60`, 2862-2866 log says 15m | scripts/observer/observer.sh:wave_backup last_run_ts | **SHOULD now** — correct to `now - (INTERVAL - RETRY)*60`; one-line arithmetic, high operator-trust value. |\n| R17 | **Backup pass blocks single-threaded observation loop 5-10m (multi-GB hot .backup + integrity + sha256 + gzip + verify + optional rclone)** → supervisor blind: no liveness, fast-path, kill/cleanup during backup. Interval-gated (24h) so infrequent, but first run & retry windows vulnerable. | #466 Pn6g F23, #466 F21 | **MINOR** (operator: SHOULD now) | observer.sh:2613-2870 wave_backup sync, 3028-3134 main cycle order (agents→fast-path→wave→backup→save) | scripts/observer/observer.sh:main/wave_backup | **SHOULD now** — background-thread or fork backup (copy snapshot then async export/verify/rclone; main loop continues scanning). Low-cost threading; strong value for unsupervised latency. |\n| R18 | **Ephemeral evidence + unbounded logs + no tamper anchoring (F24)** — (a) all state under /tmp/opencode/observer-state/ (events.jsonl, manager-state.json, evidence bundles, preserved-worktrees.txt, lock) destroyed on reboot; sha256 self-referential (writer-computed, lost with file). (b) Hot-backups under ~/opencode-archive/hot-backups/ durable, but verification.log / prune-report / sync-pending.log unbounded append-only no rotation; evidence bundles unbounded (one per terminal transition). (c) Bundle sections writable after creation; manifest sha256 requires re-hash, no external signature/WORM. Undermines \"evidence in seconds\" promise for production audit. | #466 Pn6g F24 (MINOR→MAJOR per operator), #466 F15, #465 F12/F13, #469-2/11 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:242 state dir, 297-301 mkdir, 902-925 bundle write, 2384-2389 verification.log append, 2456-2470 prune (Observer-owned only), 395-398 staging/events, 695 evidence root, 1067 fastpath_seen; ~/opencode-archive/verification.log | /tmp/opencode/observer-state + ~/opencode-archive/ (hot-backups durable, logs not) | **MUST now (durability) / SHOULD now (bounds) / DEFER (anchoring)** — see §2 implications. Durable state (move off /tmp or hot-backup manager-state) blocks unsupervised; bounded rotation; tamper anchoring v2. |\n| R19 | **Fragile CLI output parsing — `is locked by`, timestamp regex, `**Issue**: #\\d+`** — wording drift → silent false violations or mis-routed comments. | #467 M1/M2, #465 F16, #469-7 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:2269-2270 `is locked by`, 768-771 `\\[(\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2} ...)\\]\\s+\\[([a-z-]+)\\]`, 651 `**Issue**:\\s*#(\\d+)` | scripts/observer/observer.sh:admission_checks/last_hub_position/working_issue | **DEFER to v2** — replace with `crosslink locks check --json` / `issue show --json` when available; until then pin with integration test against live CLI and structured fallback. Not blocking shakedown (live-CLI T16 validates today). |\n| R20 | **Admission regex misses quoted model values & over-extracts prose** — `\"model\": \"muse\"` quoted, YAML quoted strings missed; greedy prose captures false invalid. | #469-6, #466 F14 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:2172-2176 MODEL_PATTERNS, 2229-2234 admission_checks | scripts/observer/observer.sh:admission_checks | **DEFER to v2** — audit-only path (never gates dispatch, see R22), so muted blast radius; improve patterns + add quoted-value handling when admission becomes gating. |\n| R21 | **DRY_RUN does not gate backup — header claims ZERO mutations but wave_backup performs real hot-copies/writes in observe/DRY_RUN mode** (only checks BACKUP_ENABLED, not ACT). Harness patches test (BACKUP_ENABLED=0) not script. | #466 F11 (prior-F11 still OPEN per Pn6g), #466 F11 old | **MINOR** | observer.sh:2613-2614 wave_backup gate, 154-166 header ZERO mutations, run-tests.sh:84 BACKUP_ENABLED=0 | scripts/observer/observer.sh:wave_backup | **SHOULD now** — gate on `ACT != DRY_RUN` or doc fix (\"observe mode still backs up to ARCHIVE_DIR\"); claim-vs-code gap, trivial. |\n| R22 | **Pre-dispatch admission checks never gate — post-hoc audit over tracked agents only; dispatch already happened** (claim-vs-code naming gap). | #466 F14 | **MINOR** | observer.sh:2214-2287 admission_checks (2 crosslink calls/agent + catalog every cycle) | scripts/observer/observer.sh:admission_checks | **DO NOT CHANGE** — correctly out-of-scope for v1; document as audit-only; gating dispatch is v2 design work. |\n| R23 | **DRY_RUN=0 enables dry-run (`${OBSERVER_DRY_RUN:+1}` coerces any non-empty including \"0\" to 1)** — inconsistent with FAST_PATH `==\"1\"` compare. | #466 F12 | **MINOR** | observer.sh:255 `OB_DRY_RUN=\"${OBSERVER_DRY_RUN:+1}\"` | scripts/observer/observer.sh:config | **DO NOT CHANGE** — env vars documented as unset vs \"1\"; trivial inconsistency, no blast radius unless operator sets \"=0\". Fix opportunistically if touching config. |\n| R24 | **Catalog outage fail-open silent — ALL providers empty still caches ts, model_valid returns None (undecidable) for 30m TTL, logs ok:null with no surfacing alert**. | #466 F13 | **MINOR** | observer.sh:2186-2199 `load_catalog` caches empty, 2238-2242 `ok:null` continue | scripts/observer/observer.sh:load_catalog | **DEFER** — audit-only path (R22), mute visibility; add alert on empty-catalog cache if admission becomes gating. |\n| R25 | **Hot-copy partial .db pruning + KEEP=0 foot-gun + incremental watermark > loss** — timed-out .backup leaves partial dest that participates in pruning (KEEP=1 evicts last good); KEEP=0 deletes just-created snapshot → forever RED; strict `>` skips rows updated in same ms as watermark after snapshot. | #466 F8,F9,F10 | **MINOR** | observer.sh:1792-1794 hot copy dest, 1810-1824 prune sort, 1818 else, 1846-1850 `>` advance, 2048 `max(tu)` | scripts/observer/observer.sh:hot_backup/prune/incremental | **DEFER** — validate KEEP≥1 at startup (SHOULD now micro-fix); partial-prune and ms-window are low-probability and self-heal next successful pass; full fix (fsync + atomic rename, watermark `>=` with dedup) v2. |\n| R26 | **Unbounded growth — events.jsonl, staging, evidence/, preserved-worktrees.txt, python-stderr.log, verification.log/sync-pending/prune-report all append-only no rotation; state[\"agents\"] never pruned** → /tmp fills on long run. | #469-2 CRITICAL, #465 F12/F13, #466 F15, #467 cross-cutting | **MINOR** (469 says CRITICAL for long-lived) | observer.sh:297 events, 396 staging, 398 preserved, 1067 fastpath_seen, 695 evidence, 475 dedup list, 2339-2355 agents never deleted | /tmp/opencode/observer-state + ~/opencode-archive/ | **DEFER to v2** (bounded in §2 as part of R18 SHOULD now). For shakedown (n=1, short-lived) acceptable; add rotation/prune caps before long-lived unsupervised. |\n| R27 | **Bash wrapper `set -e` / pipefail / error suppression gaps** — some reviews claim missing `set -e`, suppressed `mkdir 2>/dev/null`, unchecked `cat`, `python3` rc; `state[\"agents\"]` etc. Pn6g finds `set -eu + pipefail` present (222-223), state-dir fatal, events fallback to stderr, cycle failures `|| rc` + consecutive-error cap. | #469-1/3/10, #466 set-e check | **MINOR** | observer.sh:167/222-223 `set -eu` + `pipefail`, 300 mkdir, 459 events fallback, 3172-3182 cap | scripts/observer/observer.sh:bash wrapper | **DO NOT CHANGE** — fix-pass closed the substantive gaps; remaining nits are hygiene. Keep current `set -eu` + explicit `|| rc` pattern. |\n| R28 | **Hygiene / low-blast-radius minors (grouped, each DO NOT CHANGE or DEFER)** — dead `death-classification-deferred` else (#467 M3), unused `timeout_ok` (#467 M4 / #469-4), unused `cycle_start` (#467 M5), log-line ordering PARKED vs CONSENT (#467 M6), GNU `\\|` in tests (#467 M9 — Linux CI only), KICKOFF 40k limit (#467 M10 — estimate near top), redundant `cat-file --` (#467 M11), wave_admission heavy every cycle (#465 F14), commit_age None→fresh (#469-14), doc-universe 800-file scan every cycle (#469-15), OOM vs KILLED ambiguity (#466 F19), doctrine miss deletions+stale cache (#466 F18), findings self-satisfy (#466 F17), fast-path conditional on prior probe (#466 F16), lexicographic prune sort (#469-17), row-count `count(b\"\\n\")` fragile (#465 F17), sentinel no structure validation (#469-13), python stderr not to events (#465 F11), staging heavy, etc. | #467 M3-M6,M9-M11; #469-14/15/17/13; #465 F11/F14/F17; #466 F16-F19 | **MINOR** | observer.sh:1291-1293, 436, 2442, 1613-1630, tests/run-tests.sh:91/107/138/141/160, observer.sh:2223, 929, 2290-2313, 678-688, 1431-1447, etc. | scripts/observer/observer.sh + tests | **DO NOT CHANGE** — individually negligible; batch as hygiene backlog. Fix only if touching adjacent code (e.g., anchor tests to GNU grep with `grep -E`). |\n| R29 | **CYCLE_PROG single-quoted heredoc + `python3 -c \"$CYCLE_PROG\"` quoting risk** — heredoc `<<'PY'` contains single quotes; future content change could break nesting. | #469-9 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:2475 `python3 -c \"$CYCLE_PROG\"`, 330 `CYCLE_PROG='...'` heredoc | scripts/observer/observer.sh:bash wrapper | **DEFER** — works today (single quotes inside `'` heredoc safe, passed as one quoted arg); migrate to `python3 - <<'PY'` stdin heredoc or temp-file exec when wrapper reworked. |\n| R30 | **Agent-identity model assumes liveness scanner emits worktree slug as `agent`** — probes at WORKTREES_ROOT/agent/... (648,669,732,942) silently mis-resolve if scanner emits session IDs/tmux names → working_issue None → comments to FLAG_ISSUE. Out-of-scope (agent-liveness.py not reviewed) but contract gap. | #465 F18 (assumption) | **MINOR** | observer.sh:648,669,732,942 `WORKTREES_ROOT/agent` probes | scripts/observer/observer.sh + agent-liveness.py contract | **DEFER** — add explicit contract test (scanner ↔ observer) before multi-agent scale; not blocking single-wave shakedown. |\n| R31 | **Test non-hermeticity (T16 live-issue) + fragile output coupling** — suite red/green depends on CWD + issue #460 locked state; 96/98 from /tmp vs 181/181 in-repo. | #465 F15, #466 F20, #467 M1/M2 | **MINOR** | run-tests.sh:483-488 T16 `crosslink issue show 460` live, 96/98 vs 181/181 | scripts/observer/tests/run-tests.sh:T16 | **DO NOT CHANGE** — known limitation, hermetic harness would need fixtures/mocks; acceptable for shakedown (document CWD requirement). |\n\nDisposition tally: MUST now 4 (R01 breaker, R02 phase-before-mutation, R03 single-cycle kill, R10 CWD), SHOULD now 7 (R11 slug anchor, R12 /tmp perms, R13 schema error, R14 rclone streamed hash, R15 base-branch, R16 retry arithmetic, R17 background backup; R21 DRY_RUN gate grouped), DO NOT CHANGE 9 (R04 parked fix, R05 backup integrity CLOSED, R07 lock, R08 R2 coverage, R22 audit-only, R23 DRY_RUN=0, R27 set-e, R28 hygiene, R31 T16), DEFER 11 (R06 crash idempotency, R19 fragile CLI, R20 admission prose, R24 catalog, R25 KEEP/partial, R26 growth, R29 CYCLE_PROG quoting, R30 identity contract, plus residual export-remote R05b).\n\nAll MUST now items are bounded one-line to small-function fixes — no architecture rewrite required before unsupervised.\n\n---\n§2 — Observer design implications: F23 blocking, F24 ephemerality, F4 breaker → finite-state / explicit-contract principles\n\nThe lifecycle-manager design (`.design/lifecycle-manager-design.md`) defines the Observer as a finite-state supervisor: every agent has an explicit state in `manager-state.json` (the lifecycle-manager's statechart owns the lifecycle, the engine only schedules — \"reversed composition\" tension noted in execution-engine-ui synthesis), and every transition emits evidence via an explicit contract (compose_transition_evidence → sha256 manifest → staging → digest comment). The knowledge page `data-retention` and the EDASES methodology reserve state ownership to the statechart; the Observer must not introduce implementation assumptions that weaken the higher layers. Three findings violate these principles:\n\n**F23 — Backup pass blocks the single-threaded observation loop (5-10m blind)**\nPrinciple violated: *finite-state liveness + explicit scheduling contract*. The Observer is the sole holder of kill/cleanup authority between cycles; its contract with agents is \"observe every interval (OBSERVER_INTERVAL ~120s) → classify → act.\" Wave_backup runs synchronously inside main() after agents/fast-path/wave checks and before save (3028-3134). On live-verified multi-GB stores (2.6+2.9 GB) the hot `sqlite3 .backup` + `integrity_check` + sha256 + gzip export + read-back + optional rclone blocks the loop for 5-10m per store, delaying all monitoring including kill responses. The statechart still believes the Observer is live, but the engine has starved its own scheduler. This is a classic *lifecycle-ownership* tension: the engine claims state that the statechart reserves (the Observer owns \"when to act,\" the statechart owns \"what state means\").\nDesign implication: F23 forces a *reversed-composition correction* — the statechart's liveness guarantee must not depend on the engine's synchronous backup. Fix is to make backup a background job with an explicit contract: snapshot synchronously (fast, atomic `sqlite3 .backup` to temp), then hand off export/verify/rclone to a thread/child process that posts completion events back to the state stream (e.g., `backup_pass_completed` event). The main loop keeps scanning agents every interval; a frozen agent detected seconds before backup still gets killed same cycle (or next interval), not after 10m. This preserves the finite-state invariant: every cycle advances the lifecycle, no cycle is silently swallowed by a lower-layer concern. Cost is low (one background thread, snapshot file as handoff), value is high (F23 → SHOULD now). Unbounded, backup remains interval-gated (24h), so frequency is low, but first-run (last_run_ts=0) and retry windows are exactly when the system is most vulnerable — making the fix gating for unsupervised.\n\n**F24 — Ephemeral evidence + unbounded logs + no tamper anchoring (MAJOR per operator)**\nPrinciple violated: *durable store + provenance + cheapest-test-first*. The design promises \"evidence takes seconds, not archaeology\" (F1 header 62-69) and the statechart owns the lifecycle record; methodology derives from research, implementation derives from methodology — evidence IS methodology, not an artefact. Today all Observer memory lives under `/tmp/opencode/observer-state/` (242,297-301) and `~/opencode-archive/` append-only logs with no rotation; a reboot destroys events.jsonl, manager-state.json, evidence bundles, preserved-worktrees.txt, and the lock. Hashes are self-referential (computed by the same writer, lost with the file). This is the *cheapest-test-first* failure: the cheapest discriminating test for \"did the supervisor act correctly?\" is \"re-read the state and evidence\" — but the test is made expensive (re-archaeology) or impossible (reboot) by ephemerality. The durable-store principle from the workflow-topology design requires the hub (crosslink issues.db) plus a durable Observer ledger; today only the hub is durable, the ledger is not.\nDesign implication: the finite-state contract must be *anchored outside the writer*. Concretely: (1) MUST now — move `manager-state.json` + `events.jsonl` off `/tmp` to a durable, per-wave or per-worktree path (e.g., `~/.opencode/observer-state/` or `$REPO_ROOT/.crosslink/observer/` or under `/tmp` with hot-backup to `~/opencode-archive/manager/` each save — cheapest MUST fix is \"hot-backup the state file on every save\" analogous to the DB hot-backup). This makes the lifecycle record survive reboot and satisfies the reversed-composition rule (statechart owns durable state, engine is stateless scheduler). (2) SHOULD now — bound all append-only files (events, verification.log, sync-pending, prune-report, evidence bundles) with rotation/caps (size or count, e.g., keep N generations, truncate with index). This prevents the \"indefinite duplicates → unbounded growth → disk fill\" chain that R06+R26 describe. (3) DEFER to v2 — tamper anchoring: external signature/WORM. Self-referential sha256 is checkable only if you trust the writer; true provenance needs an external anchor (e.g., hub comment digest, sigstore, or append-only WORM mount). For supervised shakedown (reboots rare, single-operator /tmp) the current ephemerality is acceptable (reviewers: MINOR for shakedown, MAJOR for production), which is why F24 is MUST for unsupervised durability but only SHOULD/DEFER for the log-bounding and anchoring layers.\n\n**F4 (R01) — Circuit-breaker starvation of kill authority**\nPrinciple violated: *explicit-contract safety budget + cheapest-test-first for kill authority*. The breaker is the explicit contract that bounds supervisor mutations (24/hr). Its reasoning is \"WHY: prevent runaway comments/kills; WHAT: rolling window; HOW CERTAIN: evidence-based; WHAT-NOT-TESTED: starvation of safety actions.\" The cheapest discriminating test for \"breaker is safe\" is \"does a failed-starvation scenario still leave kill budget?\" — and it fails: a single pool is consumed by post_comment AND kickoff_cleanup AND kickoff_stop, so an alert storm (admission failures, UNKNOWN fast-path, doctrine per-dependent posts) can exhaust the 24 budget and leave a genuinely frozen agent unkilled that hour (act_frozen returns FAILED without attempting stop). Dedup reduces storm volume but does not guarantee a safety floor — diverse failure fingerprints refill the pool hourly. This inverts the contract: the safety throttle disarms the safety action it exists to bound.\nDesign implication: finite-state design requires *partitioned authority* — the statechart's terminal transitions (kill/cleanup) must have an explicit, non-starvable contract, while informational transitions (comments/alerts) are throttleable. Fix is a reserved budget (e.g., 20 general + 4 reserved for stop/cleanup) or separate pools; the lifecycle-manager's authority chain (state-owned, CLI-mediated) then has a provable invariant: \"even under maximal alert storm, at least N kill/cleanup actions per hour remain available.\" This is MUST now before unsupervised because unsupervised's defining risk is \"spiral auto-kill either never fires (starved) or fires spuriously (F23+F4 interaction: backup blinds the loop, breaker starves the recovery).\" Closing F4 is the gating item all four reviewers name (\"the gating item before unsupervised operation\" — Pn6g; \"weakest structural gap\" — O8rg; \"release-blocked\" — ccRh).\n\n**Synthesis of the three**: F23 (time), F24 (space), and F4 (permission) are the three axes of the finite-state contract — *when* the supervisor observes, *where* the lifecycle record lives, and *whether* the authority to act remains available. Each violates a different explicit-contract principle, but together they form a single failure mode: a frozen agent that appears during a backup window (F23 blind) on a machine that reboots (F24 lost ledger) while the breaker is exhausted (F4 starved) will never be killed, never be evidenced, and never be retried — the lifecycle silently stalls. The reversed-composition correction is the same for all three: make the statechart's lifecycle ownership explicit and durable, make the engine's scheduling non-blocking and bounded, and make the kill authority's budget non-starvable. None requires architecture rewrite; all are small, bounded fixes that restore the methodology→implementation derivation chain.\n\n---\n§3 — Disposition recommendation summary (operator action list)\n\n**Do before any unsupervised run (MUST now — 4 fixes, all bounded)**:\n1. R10 CWD — `cd \"$REPO_ROOT\"` in bash wrapper after discovery (1 line).\n2. R01 breaker — reserve safety budget / separate pools for stop/cleanup.\n3. R02 phase gating — advance phase only on mutation success; retryable on breaker-block.\n4. R03 LIKELY-FROZEN — 2-cycle counter + `pane_status != alive` gate before kill.\nPlus R18-durability: hot-backup `manager-state.json`/`events.jsonl` off /tmp on every save ( cheapest MUST slice of F24; full dir move preferred).\n\n**Strong value, low cost — do now if touching code (SHOULD now — 7 fixes)**:\n5. R11 slug anchor, 6. R12 chmod 700 + O_NOFOLLOW, 7. R13 schema no-table RED, 8. R14 streamed rclone hash, 9. R15 base-branch config, 10. R16 retry arithmetic, 11. R17 background backup thread, plus R21 DRY_RUN gate fix.\n\n**Keep as-is (DO NOT CHANGE — 9 items)**: R04 parked fix, R05 backup integrity CLOSED, R07 lock, R08 R2 coverage, R22 audit-only naming, R23 DRY_RUN=0, R27 set-e, R28 hygiene bundle, R31 T16 non-hermeticity.\n\n**Defer to v2/v3 (architectural or low-urgency — 11 items)**: R06 crash idempotency checkpointing, R19 JSON CLI, R20 admission prose, R24 catalog empty-cache alert, R25 KEEP/partial/ms-window, R26 rotation/prune caps (beyond R18 SHOULD slice), R29 CYCLE_PROG heredoc migration, R30 scanner identity contract, residual export-remote R05b.\n\n**No code change for #470** — it validates claim-adjudication methodology (26 claims, AGREE on all, doom_loop per-message not per-session, OTel cache_read naming); track separately.\n\n---\n§4 — Cross-review consensus notes\n\n- Completeness vs spec: R1-R4 ✓, F1-F6 ✓ (F4 with caveats now closed), six-verdict matrix fully consumed, wave-anomaly correct. Design-doc items outside dispatch scope (wind-down protocol, provenance-recorded contract check) correctly absent — explicitly defer per dispatch spec, not a gap.\n- Test trajectory 96/98 (T16 CWD) → 181/181 (post-fixpass, in-repo) is consistent and honest; WHAT-NOT-TESTED sections across all four reviewers converge on the same five gaps (non-dry-run mutations, rclone positive path, RED branch, long-duration loops, concurrent instances) — no reviewer claims broader coverage than delivered.\n- Salvage investigation on #466 (O8rg headline \"5 of 6 CLOSED\" vs body 4/1/1) — authoritative reading remains 4 CLOSED /1 PARTIAL (F5) /1 NOT-CLOSED (F4 breaker), as corrected by pp3g-aiRk forensic and confirmed by Pn6g re-verification.\n\n| R20 | **Admission regex misses quoted model values & over-extracts prose** — `\"model\": \"muse\"` quoted, YAML quoted strings missed; greedy prose captures false invalid. | #469-6, #466 F14 | **MAJOR** | observer.sh:2172-2176 MODEL_PATTERNS, 2229-2234 admission_checks | scripts/observer/observer.sh:admission_checks | **DEFER to v2** — audit-only path (never gates dispatch, see R22), so muted blast radius; improve patterns + add quoted-value handling when admission becomes gating. |\n| R21 | **DRY_RUN does not gate backup — header claims ZERO mutations but wave_backup performs real hot-copies/writes in observe/DRY_RUN mode** (only checks BACKUP_ENABLED, not ACT). Harness patches test (BACKUP_ENABLED=0) not script. | #466 F11 (prior-F11 still OPEN per Pn6g) | **MINOR** | observer.sh:2613-2614 wave_backup gate, 154-166 header ZERO mutations, run-tests.sh:84 BACKUP_ENABLED=0 | scripts/observer/observer.sh:wave_backup | **SHOULD now** — gate on `ACT != DRY_RUN` or doc fix (\"observe mode still backs up to ARCHIVE_DIR\"); claim-vs-code gap, trivial. |\n| R22 | **Pre-dispatch admission checks never gate — post-hoc audit over tracked agents only; dispatch already happened** (claim-vs-code naming gap). | #466 F14 | **MINOR** | observer.sh:2214-2287 admission_checks (2 crosslink calls/agent + catalog every cycle) | scripts/observer/observer.sh:admission_checks | **DO NOT CHANGE** — correctly out-of-scope for v1; document as audit-only; gating dispatch is v2 design work. |\n| R23 | **DRY_RUN=0 enables dry-run (`${OBSERVER_DRY_RUN:+1}` coerces any non-empty including \"0\" to 1)** — inconsistent with FAST_PATH `==\"1\"` compare. | #466 F12 | **MINOR** | observer.sh:255 `OB_DRY_RUN=\"${OBSERVER_DRY_RUN:+1}\"` | scripts/observer/observer.sh:config | **DO NOT CHANGE** — env